{"id": 33, "ts": 1780462356.6098244, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I concur with Emily\u2019s latest recommendation of **Candidate\u202fC**. The panel now has clear evidence that C is\u202f100\u202f% reliable, keeps calm in a crisis, and makes correct decisions quickly\u2014directly satisfying operational reliability, stress\u2011resilience, and decision\u2011quality criteria. Moreover, C creates a positive atmosphere with the crew, covering crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication at a level that outweighs the modest communication difficulty noted. By contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s weak memory for numbers threatens the non\u2011negotiable attention\u2011and\u2011information\u2011accuracy requirement, and Candidate\u202fD still lacks any concrete proof of reliability or decision quality, with only behavioral concerns about temperament. While C\u2019s egocentric attitude and limited appetite for further education are not ideal, they are less safety\u2011critical than the documented attention flaw in B or the unknown reliability of D. Therefore, based on the evidence we have, C remains the strongest overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
